<h1>{title}</h1>
<p>StackPilot AI is an early-stage software discovery prototype. Product entries are introductory research candidates—not independent endorsements or purchasing advice.</p>
<section><h2>What the advisor currently does</h2><p>The advisor matches your chosen category to the catalog. It checks team-size and budget information only where documented compatibility evidence is available. Otherwise it explicitly reports uncertainty. No AI model makes real-time purchasing decisions.</p></section>
<section><h2>Research and editorial review</h2><ol><li>Collect primary sources such as vendor documentation and official pricing pages.</li><li>Record a concrete claim, its source URL, and the date it was checked.</li><li>Compare any conflicting evidence, including region, taxes, billing period, limits, and contract terms.</li><li>Require editorial review before marking claims verified or introducing comparative fit assessments.</li><li>Review aging information again before recommending purchase decisions.</li></ol><p>Our current six catalog entries have not passed that research process. <a href="/research/">View the candidate-source research workbench</a>.</p></section>
<section><h2>Affiliate independence</h2><p>Affiliate commissions, when eventually approved, must not influence ranking scores. No affiliate tracking links are active in this prototype. We will disclose any commercial relationship at the point of recommendation and link use before activating it.</p></section>
<section><h2>Limitations</h2><p>We do not yet maintain validated prices, comprehensive feature matrices, live availability, vendor guarantees, or performance benchmarks. Always confirm critical details with the vendor before purchasing.</p></section>
